-- title:
--   Order p^{vdim G} of the Frobenius kernel ker F^v
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, let $h$ be a natural number, and let $G$ be a $p$-divisible group of height $h$ over $k$ in the sense of the structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): a family of $k$-algebras `G.level v`, $v \in \mathbb{N}$, each a commutative ring and a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $k$ that is finite and free as a $k$-module, equipped with surjective coalgebra-and-algebra maps `G.transition v : G.level (v+1) → G.level v`, such that $\dim_k \,$`G.level v` $= p^{v h}$ and the kernel of `G.transition v` is the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal of `G.level (v+1)` under multiplication by $p^v$ on the group scheme. For $v \in \mathbb{N}$ write $I_v =$ `G.augIdeal v` for the kernel of the counit of `G.level v`, and let $J_v$ be the ideal of `G.level v` generated by the set of $p^v$-th powers $a^{p^v}$ with $a \in I_v$. The assertion is that the $k$-dimension of `G.level v`$/J_v$ equals $p^{\,v \cdot n}$, where $n = \dim_k \,$`G.Cotangent 1` is the $k$-dimension of $I_1/I_1^2$.
--
--   Geometrically, $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{O}(G_v)/J_v)$ is the kernel of the $v$-th iterate of the relative Frobenius on $G$, and the statement computes its order as $p^{vn}$ with $n$ the dimension of $G$; this is the order computation in Tate's proof that the connected part of a $p$-divisible group is a divisible formal Lie group. It is used as the input over the residue field for [`PDivisibleGroup.free_cotangent_of_isArtinianRing_of_pow_eq_zero`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.free_cotangent_of_isArtinianRing_of_pow_eq_zero), which establishes freeness of the cotangent modules of a $p$-divisible group over an artinian local base.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_finrank_level_quotient_span_pow_eq_pow_mul_finrank_cotangent_one.lean

